"Sway is the mind control class."
"Sways range from single-target mind snipers to subtler manipulators."
"Most countries will not let Sways cross their borders."
"Most Sways live on Anesidora or in Allied Heroes of Earth zones."
"Sway is the class most often successfully traded."
"It usually passes from Avowed children to those less aware of its drawbacks."
"A Sway faces life as a social pariah and near-prisoner on the island."
"Sway turns up on the market at random and is snapped up quickly."
"Sways have a harder time controlling other Avowed."
"Higher-ranked Sways can usually suppress lower ones; an A-rank Sway would never be caught."
"Many Sways only befriend other Sways."
"Mind Healers repair the damage mind control leaves."
"Artonans may not mind-control human Avowed unless they are an immediate, deadly danger."
"A suspected Sway can be forced into a mind-reader's survey only after a crime in public view."
"Investigating a Sway needs an official report and convincing proof."
"Next-generation Sways get a wider selection, after the Council's complaints won more options."
"A Sway's allies must consent to their powers; sharing a profile builds trust."
"Sways are treated badly; people around them consciously ignore their anxiety."
"Some Sways work through ringing bells, instilling a suggestion over minutes of ringing."
"Sways can learn mental targeting; a panicked Sway's mental shout can reach another Sway miles off."
"Sways cannot target the dead, and high ranks resist them."
"Sways best kept apart live on a low-security residential ship miles from Anesidora."
